                "the same stem as the imperfect subjunctive + <em lang=\"es\">-re, -res, -re, -remos, -reis, -ren</em>.",
                Yo, Rows(["are", "ares", "are", "áremos", "areis", "aren"], ["iere", "ieres", "iere", "iéremos", "iereis", "ieren"], ["iere", "ieres", "iere", "iéremos", "iereis", "ieren"]),
                [("Adonde fueres, haz lo que vieres.", "When in Rome, do as the Romans do.")]),
            new("subjuntivo-futuro-perfecto", "futuro perfecto", "future perfect", true,
                "obsolete outside legal language.",
                "<em lang=\"es\">hubiere</em> etc. + past participle.",
                Yo, null,
                [("Si para entonces no hubiere pagado, …", "If by then he has not paid, … (legal)")]),
        ]),
        new("condicional", "Condicional", "conditional",
            "The mood of \"would\": polite requests, wishes, advice, guesses about the past, and the consequence in hypothetical sentences. Spanish grammars count it as a tense of the indicative.",
        [
            new("condicional-simple", "condicional simple", "conditional", false,
                "polite requests and wishes, advice, what would happen if a condition were true, and guesses about the past (<em lang=\"es\">serían las diez</em> = it must have been about ten). The condition itself takes the imperfect subjunctive: <em lang=\"es\">si tuviera tiempo, viajaría</em>.",
                "the whole infinitive + <em lang=\"es\">-ía</em> endings, with the same irregular stems as the future (<em lang=\"es\">tendría, saldría, haría</em>).",
                Yo, Whole(["ía", "ías", "ía", "íamos", "íais", "ían"], ["ía", "ías", "ía", "íamos", "íais", "ían"], ["ía", "ías", "ía", "íamos", "íais", "ían"]),
                [("Me gustaría un café, por favor.", "I would like a coffee, please."),
